FAITHFUL-PARITY NOTE (states)
  The web MetricCard is a PURE presentational component: props → <div>, no fetch, no React-Query cache, no
  Promise. It therefore has NO error / stale / offline branch — there is nothing to load, fail, age, or lose
  connectivity to. Inventing such chrome would fabricate states the source does not have and contradict the
  web spec, so this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches — exactly as the sibling presentational
  primitives BatteryDelta (0077), TimeMarker (0074), and ChartTimeRangeContext (0069) did. The real branches:
    • value     — always rendered (the headline number / string).
    • subtitle  — present or absent.
    • trend     — the legacy change pill (web `change && !delta`), the richer delta, or neither.
    • delta     — itself carries the web `<Delta>` LOADING (skeleton) and EMPTY (missing-comparison em-dash)
                  sub-states, which faithfully map the prompt's "loading" / "empty" state requirements.
    • help      — the optional "?" tooltip next to the label (present only when its body resolves).
    • icon      — the optional colored glyph box; color — one of six accents (default cyan).
  Composition seam: the web card composes the `<Delta>` and `<HelpTooltip>` ATOMIC components (owned by the
  component-library bundle, out of scope) and the allowed-files rule scopes this prompt to MetricCard.*, so
  their RENDERING is reproduced inline here. Unit-label resolution (mi/km/kWh/currency) and arbitrary i18n-key
  lookup are the units / i18n facade's job (web `useUnits()` / `t(key)`), so the delta carries already-resolved
  affixes and the help carries already-resolved copy — the same boundary the web hooks draw.

